1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:04,784
Squeeze all four and a half billion years
of Earth's history into a single day.

2
00:00:05,134 --> 00:00:08,434
Life shows up around half
past five in the morning.

3
00:00:08,484 --> 00:00:13,424
Oxygen fills the air near noon.
Animals take off after nine at night.

4
00:00:13,474 --> 00:00:17,504
The asteroid hits the dinosaurs about
twenty minutes before midnight.

5
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:21,634
And our whole species?
The last six seconds.

6
00:00:21,684 --> 00:00:25,073
Everything ever written down:
the last tenth of a second.

7
00:00:25,403 --> 00:00:28,553
This is the real thing, at true
scale: from the Earth forming,

8
00:00:28,603 --> 00:00:32,357
all the way down to a single
second, on one line you can zoom.

9
00:00:32,447 --> 00:00:34,989
It's OpenChronology, and it's free.
